    {"id": 46, "name": "Thomson spatial profile reconstruction", "module": "thomson_workflow", "function": "reconstruct_thomson_profile_from_spectra", "execution_contract": {"schema_version":"2.0","execution_level":"analysis_pipeline","completeness":"complete_with_declared_scope","input_specs":[{"name":"wavelength_nm","unit":"nm; 1-D shared or channel x wavelength 2-D","required":True},{"name":"spectra","unit":"calibrated spectral intensity; channel x wavelength","required":True},{"name":"radius_m","unit":"m; one per channel","required":True},{"name":"laser_wavelength_nm","unit":"nm","required":True},{"name":"scattering_angle_rad","unit":"rad","required":True},{"name":"instrument_response","unit":"measured normalized response matrix/kernel/callable","required":True},{"name":"signal_uncertainty","unit":"spectral intensity; pointwise 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"joint_spectral_covariance","unit":"full channel-major spectral covariance; mutually exclusive with signal_uncertainty","required":False,"description":"Full positive-definite covariance in channel-major order; mutually exclusive with signal_uncertainty. Supported by the non-collective Maxwellian and Kappa fits; not supported by the relativistic Maxwell-Juttner fit."},{"name":"model","unit":"non_collective_maxwellian, non_collective_kappa or non_collective_relativistic_maxwell_juttner","required":True,"description":"Select one of the three optical Thomson forward models explicitly; collective microwave CTS is a dedicated registered subanalysis within primary Analysis 1."},{"name":"laser_wavelength_uncertainty_nm","unit":"nm; 1-sigma","required":False,"description":"Optional 1-sigma laser-wavelength uncertainty; propagated analytically for non-collective Maxwellian/Kappa fits and by Monte Carlo for relativistic Maxwell-Juttner fits."},{"name":"scattering_angle_uncertainty_rad","unit":"rad; 1-sigma; supported for non-collective Maxwellian/Kappa and relativistic Maxwell-Juttner; mutually exclusive with beam-direction component uncertainties","required":False,"description":"Optional scalar scattering-angle uncertainty; propagated analytically for non-collective Maxwellian/Kappa fits and by Monte Carlo for relativistic Maxwell-Juttner fits. Mutually exclusive with beam-direction component uncertainties."},{"name":"instrument_response_uncertainty","unit":"response-matrix 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"instrument_response_mc_samples","unit":"count","required":False},{"name":"instrument_response_mc_min_success_fraction","unit":"dimensionless","required":False},{"name":"laser_power_w","unit":"W; incident power at scattering volume","required":False},{"name":"interaction_length_m","unit":"m","required":False},{"name":"collection_solid_angle_sr","unit":"sr","required":False},{"name":"optical_efficiency","unit":"dimensionless","required":False},{"name":"incident_polarization","unit":"dimensionless 3-vector","required":False,"description":"Required for relativistic Maxwell-Juttner forward modelling; also required for absolute-density inference."},{"name":"incident_direction","unit":"dimensionless 3-vector","required":False,"description":"Required for relativistic Maxwell-Juttner forward modelling; also required for absolute-density inference. Supply a unit 3-vector."},{"name":"scattered_direction","unit":"dimensionless 3-vector","required":False,"description":"Required for relativistic Maxwell-Juttner forward modelling; also required for absolute-density inference. Supply a unit 3-vector."},{"name":"spectral_power_density_calibrated","unit":"boolean; must be True to identify absolute density from W/nm spectra","required":False,"description":"Explicit declaration that measured spectral density is calibrated in W/nm; False by default."},{"name":"laser_power_uncertainty_W","unit":"W; 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"interaction_length_uncertainty_m","unit":"m; 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"collection_solid_angle_uncertainty_sr","unit":"sr; 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"optical_efficiency_uncertainty","unit":"dimensionless; 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"polarization_factor_uncertainty","unit":"dimensionless; 1-sigma","required":False},{"name":"density_relative_covariance","unit":"6x6 relative covariance","required":False,"description":"Per-channel (shared 6x6 or channel-specific N x 6 x 6) covariance for scattered power and five optical inputs. It does not imply cross-channel correlations; use joint_density_relative_covariance for those. It may be combined with joint_spectral_covariance and/or instrument_response_uncertainty only when its scattered-power row/column is zero; measured-power uncertainty is then supplied by spectral/response propagation. Mutually exclusive with duplicate scalar optical-factor uncertainties."},{"name":"joint_density_relative_covariance","unit":"(6*n_channels) x (6*n_channels) relative covariance","required":False,"description":"Complete channel-major covariance for the six absolute-density inversion inputs per channel, including cross-channel correlations. Available to all three Analysis 1 models when absolute-density inference is selected. It may be combined with joint_spectral_covariance and/or instrument_response_uncertainty only when all scattered-power rows/columns are zero; otherwise those sources would be double-counted. Mutually exclusive with density_relative_covariance and duplicate scalar optical-factor uncertainties."},{"name":"maximum_recoil_correction_fraction","unit":"dimensionless; maximum accepted fractional recoil-correction estimate","required":False,"default":0.01,"description":"Forwarded to the canonical optical inference engine; used only by the relativistic Maxwell-Juttner model. The implementation default is 0.01 and is a software error-budget threshold, not a universal plasma validity boundary."},{"name":"profile_reconstruction_method","unit":"text; both, pchip or smoothing_spline","required":False,"default":"both","description":"Select PCHIP, generalized-cross-validation smoothing spline, or both for each identifiable inferred radial profile."},{"name":"profile_reconstruction_points","unit":"integer; 20–5000","required":False,"default":200,"description":"Number of radial points in the reconstruction grid; restricted to the measured channel-coordinate interval."},{"name":"profile_reconstruction_mc_samples","unit":"integer; >=20","required":False,"default":200,"description":"Number of joint Monte Carlo profile draws when covariance is available."},{"name":"profile_coordinate_covariance_m2","unit":"n_channels x n_channels; m^2","required":False,"description":"Optional researcher-supplied covariance of measured channel radial coordinates; finite, symmetric and positive semidefinite. Propagated jointly with inferred profile-value uncertainty when supplied; no equilibrium or flux-coordinate mapping is inferred."},{"name":"profile_coordinate_value_cross_covariance","unit":"n_channels x n_channels; m times physical-parameter unit","required":False,"description":"Optional Cov(radius_i, inferred_parameter_j) block. Requires profile_coordinate_covariance_m2 and profile-value covariance or pointwise uncertainty. The complete joint coordinate/value block covariance must be positive semidefinite and is sampled jointly; no missing cross-covariance is inferred."},{"name":"joint_spatial_spectral","unit":"boolean","required":False,"default":False,"description":"When True, dispatch to a joint wavelength-resolved spatial inverse using the explicitly selected Maxwellian, finite-variance Kappa or relativistic Maxwell-Juttner model. The relativistic branch supports optional single-scattering Compton recoil."},{"name":"spatial_mixing_matrix","unit":"dimensionless fixed detector-channel x spatial-node forward operator","required":False,"description":"Required when joint_spatial_spectral is True. Researcher-supplied fixed non-negative mixing matrix; TIS does not estimate or calibrate a PSF."},{"name":"spatial_regularization_strength","unit":"non-negative numerical curvature-penalty strength","required":False,"default":0,"description":"User-selected curvature penalty for log-Te, projected flow and log-amplitude profiles in the joint spatial-spectral inverse; not a physical parameter or automatically tuned prior."},{"name":"kappa_index","unit":"dimensionless; >1.5; optimizer seed or fixed model parameter","required":False,"description":"Required for joint Kappa inference; acts as a numerical seed when fit_kappa_index is True and as a fixed external model parameter otherwise."},{"name":"fit_kappa_index","unit":"boolean","required":False,"default":False,"description":"For joint Kappa inference, whether the Kappa index is inferred from measured spectra or held fixed at kappa_index."},{"name":"radial_order","unit":"integer; >=12","required":False,"default":24,"description":"Relativistic Maxwell-Juttner quadrature order in the joint spatial-spectral forward model."},{"name":"angular_order","unit":"integer; >=8","required":False,"default":12,"description":"Relativistic Maxwell-Juttner angular quadrature order in the joint spatial-spectral forward model."},{"name":"maximum_recoil_correction_fraction","unit":"dimensionless; maximum accepted fractional recoil-correction estimate","required":False,"default":0.01,"description":"Relativistic Maxwell-Juttner only; no-recoil error-budget screen when include_compton_recoil is False."},{"name":"include_compton_recoil","unit":"boolean","required":False,"default":False,"description":"Relativistic Maxwell-Juttner only; enables single-scattering Compton recoil and polarized Klein-Nishina weighting in joint spatial-spectral inference."}],"output_specs":[{"name":"electron_temperature_profile_eV","unit":"eV"},{"name":"electron_density_profile_m3","unit":"m^-3","description":"Only where identifiable from selected model and supplied calibration/geometry."},{"name":"electron_velocity_projection_profile_m_s","unit":"m s^-1"},{"name":"channels","unit":"structured","description":"Per-channel fit, residuals, covariance, assumptions and provenance."},{"name":"electron_temperature_uncertainty_profile_eV","unit":"eV"},{"name":"electron_density_uncertainty_profile_m3","unit":"m^-3"},{"name":"electron_velocity_projection_uncertainty_profile_m_s","unit":"m s^-1","description":"Per-channel uncertainty of the fitted non-collective projection; in collective mode available when supplied flow-vector and/or beam-geometry uncertainties are propagated by Monte Carlo."},{"name":"joint_inference","unit":"structured","description":"Joint GLS parameters, covariance and fit diagnostics when joint_spectral_covariance is supplied."},{"name":"model_discrepancy_covariance","unit":"parameter covariance","description":"Residual-based model-adequacy covariance, only when a supported reduced chi-square and fit covariance are available."},{"name":"electron_density_joint_covariance_m6","unit":"n_channels x n_channels; m^-6","description":"Full cross-channel absolute-density covariance propagated from joint_density_relative_covariance."},{"name":"electron_density_cross_channel_covariance_available","unit":"boolean"},{"name":"spatial_profile_reconstruction","unit":"structured","description":"PCHIP and/or GCV smoothing-spline reconstructions of every identifiable spectrum-inferred parameter profile, including kappa index when supported; no extrapolation beyond measured channel coordinates."},{"name":"methods","unit":"structured mapping","description":"Per-method result for PCHIP and/or GCV smoothing spline, including status, reconstructed values, gradients, uncertainty bands and method metadata."},{"name":"covariance_model","unit":"text","description":"States full supplied cross-channel covariance, independent pointwise uncertainty fallback, or unavailable covariance."},{"name":"extrapolation","unit":"text","description":"Explicitly reports that reconstruction is forbidden outside the measured coordinate interval."},{"name":"uncertainty_mc_successful_samples","unit":"integer; per method","description":"Number of valid joint covariance draws used for each reconstructed profile."},{"name":"uncertainty_warning","unit":"text; conditional","description":"Explains when too few valid covariance draws prevent uncertainty bands."},{"name":"parameter_identifiability","unit":"structured primary/conditional/non-identifiable classification","description":"Explicitly separates parameters identifiable directly from this calibrated measurement, parameters conditional on additional supplied quantities, and parameters non-identifiable under the selected model."},{"name":"smoothing_diagnostics","unit":"structured; per reconstructed profile and method","description":"For full supplied cross-channel covariance, reports GLS-GCV smoothing parameter, effective degrees of freedom, generalized residual sum of squares and system conditioning. Singular covariance is rejected rather than silently regularized."},{"name":"primary_result_status","unit":"text; identified_from_measured_data or not_identifiable_from_measured_data","description":"Joint spatial-spectral mode reports data-only Jacobian identifiability separately from optimizer convergence."},{"name":"primary_outputs_reportable_as_identified","unit":"boolean","description":"False when the measured-data Jacobian is rank deficient or the optimizer did not converge; regularization rows do not count as independent measurements."},{"name":"optimizer","unit":"structured","description":"Includes optimizer convergence, data-only Jacobian rank and conditioning; regularization rows are excluded from the identifiability rank."},{"name":"optimizer_candidate","unit":"structured; non-primary diagnostic result","description":"Numerical candidate profiles and regularized covariance retained only for troubleshooting when the data-only inverse is rank deficient or the optimizer fails; these values are explicitly not measured primary outputs."}],"assumptions":["Input spectra and wavelength axes are measured and calibrated; this workflow does not calibrate the diagnostic.","Spatial coordinates are supplied for each measured spectral channel.","The selected physical model is explicit and is the same model used by the canonical spectrum-to-parameter inference.","Non-collective Maxwellian and kappa models use isotropic projected electron distributions; kappa is a parameterized finite-variance model, not an unrestricted VDF inversion.","The relativistic Maxwell-Juttner model assumes an isotropic rest-frame distribution and bulk flow parallel to the scattering vector; elastic Thomson scattering is the default, with optional single-scattering Compton recoil and polarized Klein-Nishina weighting.","Absolute density requires calibrated W/nm spectral intensity and complete optical geometry/polarization inputs.","Profile reconstruction is restricted to the measured channel-coordinate interval and does not extrapolate."],"preprocessing":["Validate finite channel-by-wavelength arrays, channel-to-radius correspondence and strictly increasing calibrated wavelength axes without sorting, repairing or dropping source samples.","Apply the supplied instrument response in bin-integrated spectral-power space using calibrated wavelength-bin widths, then convert back to spectral density; 1-D index kernels require a uniform wavelength grid."],"algorithm":"Infer per-channel electron temperature and supported scattering-vector flow from measured calibrated optical Thomson spectra using the selected non-collective Maxwellian, Kappa or relativistic Maxwell-Juttner forward model. Infer absolute density only when calibrated W/nm intensity and complete optical geometry are supplied; reconstruct identifiable radial profiles only within the measured channel interval. Optional joint_spatial_spectral mode directly fits channel-by-wavelength calibrated measurements through a researcher-supplied fixed spatial mixing operator using the selected isotropic Maxwellian, finite-variance Kappa or relativistic Maxwell-Juttner model; the relativistic joint model supports optional single-scattering Compton recoil and polarized Klein-Nishina weighting. In joint spatial-spectral mode, data identifiability is assessed from the measured-data Jacobian alone; optional regularization rows are excluded so smoothing cannot manufacture independent measurement constraints.","uncertainty_model":"The wrapper forwards the measured spectra and all supported uncertainty inputs to the canonical Thomson inference engine. Non-collective Maxwellian and Kappa fits support local covariance and full channel-major GLS; relativistic Maxwell-Juttner uses channel-local covariance plus Monte Carlo propagation of laser-wavelength, scalar-angle or beam-direction, incident-polarization and response-matrix uncertainties, but not full channel-major spectral GLS. Collective CTS retains its own branch-specific uncertainty contract. Absolute-density uncertainty combines the supported spectral/response and optical-factor covariance sources without double counting when scattered-power covariance rows/columns are zero. Profile covariance is propagated from the available fit and input covariance only; no experimental validation is claimed. Profile smoothing uses full supplied cross-channel covariance in a GLS objective when available; Monte Carlo bands remain conditional on the supplied/inferred covariance. Joint spatial-spectral covariance is conditional on the selected regularization and fixed forward operators; the data-only Jacobian rank is reported separately from the regularized optimizer Jacobian.","limitations":["Relativistic Maxwell-Juttner inference is restricted to an isotropic rest-frame distribution with bulk flow parallel to the scattering vector and neglects recoil/Compton corrections. The dedicated multichannel GLS API assumes common Te, q-parallel flow, wavelength grid and geometry across channels.","Kappa models are parameterized distributions and do not reconstruct an unrestricted electron velocity distribution.","Absolute density is not identifiable from normalized spectral shape alone; it requires W/nm intensity and complete optical geometry/polarization inputs.","Joint full-channel GLS is implemented for non-collective Maxwellian and Kappa models only; the relativistic Maxwell-Juttner model uses its declared channel-local covariance path.","Profile reconstruction does not extrapolate beyond the measured radial interval; unresolved or non-identifiable parameters are reported as such.","No independent experimental validation is claimed.","Optical collective dielectric inference is outside the current Analysis 1 model shortlist; microwave CTS is a dedicated registered subanalysis within primary Analysis 1.","Full-covariance GLS smoothing requires a positive-definite cross-channel covariance; singular covariance is explicitly rejected without regularization.","Joint spatial-spectral inversion supports isotropic Maxwellian, finite-variance Kappa and relativistic Maxwell-Juttner parameterizations; it does not reconstruct an arbitrary EVDF. Geometry, spatial mixing and response operators remain fixed external inputs.","In joint spatial-spectral mode, regularization can select a numerical profile in an underdetermined problem but cannot make that profile data-identifiable; inspect primary_result_status and data_only_jacobian_rank."],"function_links":["tokamak_analysis.thomson_workflow.reconstruct_thomson_profile_from_spectra","tokamak_analysis.thomson_workflow.reconstruct_thomson_joint_spatial_spectra","tokamak_analysis.thomson_joint_spatial_spectral.reconstruct_joint_thomson_spatial_spectra"],"raw_data_to_physics":False,"note":"This registered profile subanalysis consumes measured calibrated optical Thomson spectra and delegates to the canonical physical forward model. It never accepts pre-derived ne/Te profiles.","workflow_modes":[{"name":"spatial_profile_from_measured_spectra","function":"tokamak_analysis.thomson_workflow.reconstruct_thomson_profile_from_spectra","inputs":["wavelength_nm","spectra (channel × wavelength)","radius_m","laser_wavelength_nm","scattering_angle_rad","instrument_response","optional uncertainty/covariance and explicit model inputs"],"outputs":["electron_temperature_profile_eV","electron_density_profile_m3 where identifiable","electron_velocity_projection_profile_m_s","per-channel fit diagnostics"],"scope":"Profile-oriented output from the canonical measured calibrated spectrum-to-physics inference; no pre-derived profile input."}],"completion_scope":"Profile-oriented output from the canonical measured-calibrated optical Thomson spectrum-to-physics inference using the three selected non-collective models. PCHIP and generalized-cross-validation spline reconstruction are restricted to the measured radial interval; no pre-derived ne/Te profile points are accepted. Microwave collective CTS remains a dedicated subanalysis within primary Analysis 1. No independent experimental validation is claimed.","calibrated_measurements_to_physics":True}},
